s argue for measuring 'workflow fidelity' - how well an agent follows intended processes - which is crucial for financial and other high-stakes applications of AI coding agents.\",\n    \"author\": \"Donghao Huang, Joon Kiat Chua, Zhaoxia Wang\",\n    \"source\": \"Paper\",\n    \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.06457\",\n    \"published_date\": \"2026-05-08\",\n    \"topics\": [\"ai-agents\", \"evaluation\", \"workflow-fidelity\", \"fintech\", \"llm\"],\n    \"type\": \"technical\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"title\": \"Automated Alignment is Harder Than You Think\",\n    \"description\": \"Paper submitted May 8, 2026, examining challenges in automating AI alignment. The authors demonstrate fundamental difficulties in creating automated systems that can reliably align AI behavior with human values, with implications for AI coding tools that need to maintain safety and security while remaining useful.\",\n    \"author\": \"Aleksandr Bowkis, Marie Davidsen Buhl, Jacob Pfau, Geoffrey Irving\",\n    \"source\": \"Paper\",\n    \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.06390\",\n    \"published_date\": \"2026-05-08\",\n    \"topics\": [\"ai-safety\", \"alignment\", \"automation\", \"ethics\", \"research\"],\n    \"type\": \"technical\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"title\": \"Karpathy on 'From Vibe Coding to Agentic Engineering' at AI Ascent 2026\",\n    \"description\": \"At AI Ascent 2026, Andrej Karpathy discussed how 'vibe coding' has evolved over the past year. He explained the shift from one-shot prompt coding toward agentic engineering workflows, noting that programming has become 'unrecognizable' compared to just a year ago. The talk covered code agents, AutoResearch, and what Karpathy calls the 'Loopy Era of AI.'\",\n    \"author\": \"Andrej Karpathy\",\n    \"source\": \"YouTube\",\n    \"url\": \"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=96jN2OCOfLs\",\n    \"published_date\": \"2026-05-07\",\n    \"topics\": [\"vibe-coding\", \"agentic-engineering\", \"ai-coding\", \"karpathy\", \"ai-ascent\"],\n    \"type\": \"opinion\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"title\": \"Y Combinator's Stake in OpenAI Revealed\",\n    \"description\": \"John Gruber revealed that Y Combinator owns approximately 0.6% of OpenAI, which at OpenAI's current $852 billion valuation is worth over $5 billion. This information was difficult to obtain and came from sources familiar with OpenAI investors.\",\n    \"author\": \"John Gruber (covered by Simon Willison)\",\n    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n    \"url\": \"https://daringfireball.net/linked/2026/05/05/y-combinator-openai-stake\",\n    \"published_date\": \"2026-05-05\",\n    \"topics\": [\"openai\", \"y-combinator\", \"ai\", \"investment\", \"valuation\"],\n    \"type\": \"opinion\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"title\": \"Granite 4.1 LLMs Released by IBM with Apache 2.0 License\",\n    \"description\": \"IBM released the Granite 4.1 family of LLMs (3B, 8B, 30B sizes) under Apache 2.0 license. Simon Willison conducted an experiment testing 'Generate an SVG of a pelican riding a bicycle' across 21 different quantized variants ranging from 1.2GB to 6.34GB. Results showed no clear pattern relating model size to output quality - all performed poorly at the specific task.\",\n    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/2026/May/4/granite-pelican/\",\n    \"published_date\": \"2026-05-04\",\n    \"topics\": [\"ibm\", \"ai\", \"generative-ai\", \"llms\", \"llm-release\", \"quantization\", \"evaluation\"],\n    \"type\": \"technical\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"title\": \"Redis Arrays Feature Built with AI Assistance\",\n    \"description\": \"Salvatore Sanfilippo submitted a PR adding a new array data type to Redis with commands like ARCOUNT, ARDEL, ARGET, ARGREP, etc. The ARGREP command can run server-side grep using the TRE regex library. Simon Willison used Claude Code to build an interactive playground for testing these new commands in a WASM-compiled build of Redis running in the browser. Salvatore documented the AI-assisted development process in 'Redis array type: short story of a long development.'\",\n    \"author\": \"Simon Willison, Salvatore Sanfilippo\",\n    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/2026/May/4/redis-arrays/\",\n    \"published_date\": \"2026-05-04\",\n    \"topics\": [\"redis\", \"databases\", \"ai-assisted-programming\", \"claude-code\", \"regex\"],\n    \"type\": \"technical\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"title\": \"iNaturalist Sightings Feature Built Entirely on Phone with Claude Code\",\n    \"description\": \"Simon Willison built a new 'Sightings' feature for his blog using Claude Code for web on his phone while camping. The feature displays wildlife photos from iNaturalist with filters, search, and RSS feed. He back-populated over a decade of iNaturalist observations, making photos searchable (e.g., lemur photos from Madagascar 2019). The entire feature - from Python CLI for fetching observations to the HTML interface - was built using AI assistance.\",\n    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/2026/May/2/sightings/\",\n    \"published_date\": \"2026-05-02\",\n    \"topics\": [\"blogging\", \"photography\", \"wildlife\", \"ai\", \"inaturalist\", \"generative-ai\", \"llms\", \"ai-assisted-programming\", \"claude-code\"],\n    \"type\": \"tutorial\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"title\": \"AI Code Generation Adoption Exceeds 85% in 2026\",\n    \"description\": \"Reports indicate that AI code generation adoption has exceeded 85% in 2026. The market is shifting from simple code completion to full-process automation. Key trends include: Agentic Coding era where AI evolves from helpers to engineering participants, enterprise-grade security becoming a priority, and multi-scenario tool specialization for enterprise vs. individual vs. cloud-native development.\",\n    \"author\": \"Various Industry Reports\",\n    \"source\": \"TechMedia\",\n    \"url\": \"https://developer.baidu.com/article/detail.html?id=5597538\",\n    \"published_date\": \"2026-05-01\",\n    \"topics\": [\"ai-coding\", \"llms\", \"adoption\", \"enterprise\", \"automation\", \"developer-tools\"],\n    \"type\": \"technical\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"title\": \"2026 AI Programming Tools Competitive Landscape Shifting\",\n    \"description\": \"The AI programming tools market in 2026 is led by Cursor, GitHub Copilot, and Windsurf, with emerging open-source Coding Agent projects gaining traction. The landscape now includes four major categories: terminal-native agents, IDE extension plugins, AI-native IDE forks, and complex engineering orchestration platforms.\",\n    \"author\": \"51CTO\",\n    \"source\": \"TechMedia\",\n    \"url\": \"https://www.51cto.com/article/838572.html\",\n    \"published_date\": \"2026-05-01\",\n    \"topics\": [\"ai-coding\", \"developer-tools\", \"market-analysis\", \"ide\", \"automation\"],\n    \"type\": \"technical\"\n  }\n]\n",
